latest_plan = "Based on our reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Initialize the Grid:\n   - Create a new grid of the same size as the input grid, initially filled with zeros (black).\n\n2. Identify Color Points:\n   - Scan the input grid and create a list of all non-zero color points, storing their row, column, and color value.\n   - Sort this list from top to bottom, then left to right. This ensures we process higher points first.\n\n3. Draw Vertical Lines:\n   - For each color point in the sorted list:\n     a. Extend upwards from the point until hitting another color or the top edge of the grid.\n     b. Extend downwards from the point until hitting another color or the bottom edge of the grid.\n   - When extending, if a cell is already colored, stop the line for that direction.\n\n4. Draw Horizontal Lines:\n   - For each color point in the sorted list:\n     a. Extend left from the point until hitting a different color or the left edge of the grid.\n     b. Extend right from the point until hitting a different color or the right edge of the grid.\n   - When extending, if a cell is already colored with a different color, stop the line for that direction.\n\n5. Preserve Original Colors:\n   - Iterate through the input grid. For any non-zero color in the input grid, set the corresponding cell in the new grid to that color.\n\n6. Fill Remaining Black Cells:\n   - Scan the new grid for any remaining black (0) cells.\n   - For each black cell:\n     a. Look upwards for the nearest non-black color. If found, fill the current cell with this color.\n     b. If no color is found above, look left for the nearest non-black color and fill the current cell with this color.\n\n7. Final Check:\n   - Perform a final scan of the grid to ensure no black cells remain.\n   - If any black cells are found, fill them with the nearest non-black color (checking up and left as in step 6).\n\n8. Return the New Grid:\n   - The resulting grid should now be the solution to the challenge.\n\nThis plan follows the pattern we identified in our reflection:\n- It prioritizes vertical lines (steps 3 and 4).\n- It respects the top-down priority for conflicting vertical lines (due to the sorting in step 2).\n- It draws horizontal lines after vertical lines (step 4).\n- It preserves original color points (step 5).\n- It fills remaining black cells with the nearest color, prioritizing above then left (steps 6 and 7).\n\nBy following this plan, we should be able to solve all the test cases and meet the challenge requirements."
